hadiths[11]{hadithnumber,text}:
"577","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: When Surah Al-Ma'idah was revealed, I was holding the reins of Al-Adba' (the she-camel), and it was so heavy that my arm was about to be cut off because of its weight."
"578","Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: I read the verse « فَمِنْهَا رَكُوبُهُمْ وَمِنْهَا يَأْكُلُونَ » [36-يس:72] of Surah Ya-Sin in the Mushaf of Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) as follows: « فَمِنْهَا رَكُوعَبُتُهُمْ وَمِنْهَا يَأْكُلُونَ » ."
"579","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): A man asked him, ""What was the intention of Yusuf (peace be upon him)?"" So he (Ibn Abbas) mentioned something, but we did not remember it. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Yusuf (peace be upon him) looked at the roof of the house, and he saw Yaqub (peace be upon him) holding his hand and saying, ""Do you want to do the deed of the ignorant while your name is written among the Prophets (peace be upon them)?"" So (upon hearing this), every kind of desire that was in his body left him, and he ran towards the door, and she also ran after him and tore his shirt."
"580","Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked about the ""incident"" of Yusuf (peace be upon him), what was it? (To what extent did it reach?) He replied: He had untied his waistband, then a voice was called out to him which was not heard, so it was said to him: O son of Yaqub! Do you intend to commit adultery? You will become like that bird which plucks out its own feathers and then has no feathers left."
"581","Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated: It was asked from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about children, whether they will be in Paradise. He replied: Musa and Khidr (peace be upon them) debated about this matter, and that is sufficient for you."
"582","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said in the explanation of Allah Almighty’s statement: “A witness from her own people testified,” that he was a special person of the king."
"583","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: He had a beard."
"584","Abdur Razzaq narrated: Isra'il (Ibn Yunus bin Abi Ishaq) informed us with the same wording through this chain of narration."
"585","Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding the prostration in Surah Sad: He said: It is the repentance of a servant or the repentance of a prophet. So Allah commanded Muhammad (peace be upon him) to follow him in this."
"586","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: Allah made it obligatory upon them that one should fight against ten, so this was burdensome and difficult for them, then Allah removed this (hardship, burden) from them and commanded that one should fight and face two, so Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: « إِن يَكُن مِّنكُمْ عِشْرُونَ صَابِرُونَ يَغْلِبُوا مِائَتَيْنِ » ""If there are twenty steadfast among you, they will overcome two hundred."" And then he recited till the end of the verses. Then he said: « لَّوْلَا كِتَابٌ مِّنَ اللَّهِ سَبَقَ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِيمَا أَخَذْتُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ » ""If it had not been for a prior decree from Allah, you would have been severely punished for what you have taken."" Meaning the spoils of Badr, He says: My way is that I do not punish the one who disobeys Me until I have given him prior warning. Then He said: « يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ قُل لِّمَن فِي أَيْدِيكُم مِّنَ الْأَسْرَىٰ إِن يَعْلَمِ اللَّهُ فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ خَيْرًا » ""O Prophet! Say to those captives who are in your hands, if Allah knows any good in your hearts..."" Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This verse was revealed about me when I informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about my Islam, and requested him not to hold me accountable for the twenty uqiyah he had taken from me, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave me twenty slaves, all of whom traded with the wealth that was in your possession, and along with that, stored up forgiveness from Allah."
"587","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the Battle of Badr, it was said to him: You should pursue this trade caravan, there is nothing else. So Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) called out to them, while he was in his bonds (he had been tied with rope), that it is not permissible for you, so he (the Prophet) said: Why (is it not permissible)? He (Abbas) said: Because Allah had promised you one of the two groups, and He has fulfilled for you what He had promised you."
